[1mNAME[0m
    roffsub - check, compile, and render
    terminal manuals written in roffsub

[1mSYNOPSIS[0m
    [1mroffsub[0m [[1m-w[0m [4mwidth[0m] [[1m-s[0m [4mstyle[0m] [[1m-m[0m [4mmeasure[0m] [[4mfile[0m]
    [1mroffsub[0m [1m-e[0m [[1m-s[0m [4mstyle[0m] [[4mfile[0m]
    [1mroffsub[0m [1m-c[0m [4mfile[0m ...
    [1mroffsub[0m [1m-i[0m [[1m-d[0m [4mdate[0m] [[1m-r[0m [4mrev[0m] [[4mfile[0m]
    [1mroffsub[0m [1m-p[0m [[1m-w[0m [4mwidth[0m] [[4mfile[0m]
    [1mroffsub[0m [1m-g[0m [1mc[0m|[1mbash[0m [4mname[0m [[4mfile[0m]
    [1mroffsub[0m [1m-n[0m [[1m-d[0m [4mdate[0m] [[1m-r[0m [4mrev[0m] [[4mfile[0m]
    [1mroffsub[0m [1m-h[0m | [1m--help[0m | [1m-V[0m

[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
    [1mroffsub[0m works with manuals written
    in roffsub, a subset of the man
    macros and tbl that every roff
    program displays and that small awk
    and C routines can also render. It
    renders a manual for the terminal in
    use, at that terminal's width, with
    bold and italic where the terminal
    can show them. It also checks a
    manual's form, compiles it into
    records, formats it at a fixed
    width, and writes the text as a C
    array or a bash heredoc for a
    program to carry.

    [1mroffsub[0m comes as a C binary and as a
    bash function that behave alike. The
    function serves systems where
    programs cannot be run from the
    user's own directories, such as a
    home directory mounted noexec, so
    one package works everywhere. Both
    use awk to check, compile, and
    generate; the binary renders records
    and pre-formatted text without it.

[1mOPTIONS[0m
    [1m-w[0m [4mwidth[0m
        Render at [4mwidth[0m columns. Without
        it the width comes from
        [1mMANWIDTH[0m, then from the
        terminal, then 80; output that
        is not a terminal is 80 columns
        unless [1mMANWIDTH[0m is set.

    [1m-s[0m [4mstyle[0m
        Write emphasis as [1mplain[0m (none),
        [1moverstrike[0m (backspace sequences
        for a pager), [1msgr[0m (terminal
        control sequences), or [1mpre[0m (font
        escapes for later emission).
        Without it the style follows the
        destination; see [1mOUTPUT[0m [1mCHOICES[0m.

    [1m-m[0m [4mmeasure[0m
        Never fill text past [4mmeasure[0m
        columns, however wide the
        terminal.

    [1m-e[0m  Emit pre-formatted text, as
        written by [1m-p[0m, in the chosen
        style.

    [1m-c[0m  Check the form of each [4mfile[0m and
        report every departure from
        roffsub as [4mfile[0m:[4mline[0m: [4mid[0m:
        [4mmessage[0m. The exit status is 1
        when an error was found. With
        [1mROFFSUB_STRICT[0m set, warnings
        count as errors too.

    [1m-i[0m  Write the compiled records of
        [4mfile[0m. [1m-d[0m and [1m-r[0m fill in [1m@DATE@[0m
        and [1m@VERSION@[0m on the [1m.TH[0m line.

    [1m-p[0m  Write [4mfile[0m formatted at a fixed
        width (default 80) with its font
        changes kept, for a program's
        [1mpreformatted[0m profile.

    [1m-g[0m [1mc[0m|[1mbash[0m [4mname[0m
        Write the lines of [4mfile[0m as a C
        array called [4mname[0m, or as a
        marked bash region that reads
        them into the variable [4mname[0m.

    [1m-n[0m  Write [4mfile[0m as the page to
        install for man. [1m-d[0m and [1m-r[0m fill
        in the [1m.TH[0m line as for [1m-i[0m, and
        each table is rewritten so that
        roff draws it as roffsub does:
        no vertical lines, and a + where
        a rule meets a column gap. The
        source itself stays as written.

    [1m-h[0m  Print the usage summary.

    [1m--help[0m
        Show this manual.

    [1m-V[0m  Print the version.

    A [4mfile[0m may be a roffsub source or
    its compiled records; records begin
    with the line [1mv[0m, a tab, and [1m1[0m.
    Without a [4mfile[0m the standard input is
    read.

[1mOUTPUT CHOICES[0m
    [1mOUTPUT[0m: terminal
    [1mGOES[0m [1mTO[0m: the pager
    [1mSTYLE[0m: overstrike
    [1mWIDTH[0m: terminal

    [1mOUTPUT[0m: terminal, PAGER is cat
    [1mGOES[0m [1mTO[0m: the terminal
    [1mSTYLE[0m: sgr
    [1mWIDTH[0m: terminal

    [1mOUTPUT[0m: file or pipe
    [1mGOES[0m [1mTO[0m: the file or pipe
    [1mSTYLE[0m: plain
    [1mWIDTH[0m: 80

    The pager is [1mPAGER[0m when set,
    otherwise [1mless[0m when installed,
    otherwise [1mmore[0m. [1mTERM=dumb[0m selects
    plain. Command-line options override
    the environment, and the environment
    overrides these defaults.

[1mENVIRONMENT[0m
    [1mMANWIDTH[0m
        The rendering width.

    [1mCOLUMNS[0m
        The terminal width, when
        [1mMANWIDTH[0m is not set.

    [1mPAGER[0m
        The pager for terminal output.

    [1mROFFSUB_STYLE[0m
        The style: plain, overstrike,
        sgr, or pre.

    [1mROFFSUB_SGR[0m
        Control sequence parameters for
        bold and italic, as
        [1mb=1;33:i=4;36[0m. The defaults are
        1 (bold) and 4 (underline).
        Colors let bold and italic show
        as distinct colors.

    [1mROFFSUB_MEASURE[0m
        The maximum line length.

    [1mROFFSUB_HEADING[0m
        The number of columns section
        headings are moved in from the
        margin; 0 by default. Everything
        else stays in place.

    [1mROFFSUB_STRICT[0m
        When set, the check treats
        warnings as errors.

[1mEXIT STATUS[0m
    0 on success, 1 when a check found
    errors, 2 on a usage or input error.

[1mEXAMPLES[0m
    Check a manual, then read it as a
    program would show it:

    roffsub -c srt.1
    roffsub srt.1
    roffsub -w 50 -s plain srt.1 > srt.txt

    Embed the full manual in a C program
    and in a bash function:

    roffsub -i -d 2026-11-15 -r r0.9 srt.1 > srt.ir
    roffsub -g c srt_man srt.ir > srt.man.h
    roffsub -g bash _srt_man srt.ir > srt.man.bash

    Write the page to install:

    roffsub -n -d 2026-11-15 -r r0.9 srt.1 > srt.1.out

    Embed a pre-formatted manual in a
    small program:

    roffsub -p srt.1 > srt.pre
    roffsub -g c srt_man srt.pre > srt.man.h

